---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/indas/indas8.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Applicability" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Selecting & Applying Accounting Policies" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Changes in Accounting Policies — Retrospective Application" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Changes in Accounting Estimates — Prospective Application" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Prior Period Errors — Retrospective Restatement" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Indian Restatement Practice & Schedule III Interaction" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Impracticability Exception" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Ind AS 8 vs IAS 8 — Full Comparison" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Quick-Reference Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ============ SECTION 1 — CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK LINKAGE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Identical hierarchy and treatment distinctions to IAS 8</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 8 applies the IDENTICAL framework as IAS 8 — a defined HIERARCHY for selecting accounting policies absent a specific Ind AS, and a clear distinction between POLICY CHANGES/ERRORS (retrospective) and ESTIMATE CHANGES (prospective).</div>
        <div class="elabel">HOW IND AS 8 MAPS TO THE FRAMEWORK</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span><strong>Comparability</strong> — retrospective restatement for policy changes/errors preserves comparability across periods — identical to IAS 8</span>
          <span><strong>Faithful representation</strong> — prospective treatment for estimate changes reflects that estimates are refinements based on new information, not corrections of past mistakes — identical to IAS 8</span>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Ind AS 8 introduced NO substantive change to this framework relative to IAS 8 — its practical Indian relevance lies mainly in how restatements interact with Schedule III's prescribed comparative presentation format.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">The three scenarios — identical treatment to IAS 8</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-13-1"><span>Scenario</span><span>Treatment</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-13-1"><span>Change in accounting policy</span><span>RETROSPECTIVE (restate prior periods)</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-13-1"><span>Change in accounting estimate</span><span>PROSPECTIVE (current and future periods only)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-13-1"><span>Prior period error</span><span>RETROSPECTIVE (restate as if error never occurred)</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 2 — SCOPE & DEFINITIONS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope &amp; Applicability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw"><div class="ctitle cw">What Ind AS 8 covers</div><div class="principle">Ind AS 8 prescribes criteria for selecting/changing accounting policies, and the accounting/disclosure of changes in estimates and error corrections — IDENTICAL scope to IAS 8.</div></div>
      <div class="card cd"><div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions you must know</div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Prior period errors</div><div class="glossary-def">IDENTICAL definition to IAS 8 — omissions/misstatements from failure to use, or misuse of, reliable information available when prior period statements were authorised for issue.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Retrospective application</div><div class="glossary-def">Applying a new policy as if it had always been applied — identical concept to IAS 8.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 3 — SELECTING & APPLYING ACCOUNTING POLICIES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Selecting &amp; Applying Accounting Policies</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Identical hierarchy to IAS 8</div><div class="text-supporting">Where no specific Ind AS applies, management uses judgement to develop a policy that is relevant and reliable, referring first to requirements in Ind ASs dealing with similar issues, then the Framework — IDENTICAL hierarchy to IAS 8.</div></div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 4 — CHANGES IN ACCOUNTING POLICIES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Changes in Accounting Policies — Retrospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Identical retrospective mechanics to IAS 8</div>
      <div class="worked worked--flush"><div class="wk-title">Example 1: A voluntary change in inventory valuation method</div><div class="wk-body">An Indian company voluntarily changes its inventory cost formula from weighted average to FIFO, concluding the new policy provides more reliable and relevant information, with a cumulative effect of ₹40,00,000 higher opening retained earnings.</div><div class="wk-answer">The change is applied RETROSPECTIVELY — prior period comparatives are RESTATED as if FIFO had always been used, and the ₹40,00,000 cumulative adjustment is recognised in OPENING RETAINED EARNINGS of the earliest period presented — an IDENTICAL mechanism to how IAS 8 would treat the same voluntary policy change globally.</div></div>
    </div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 5 — CHANGES IN ACCOUNTING ESTIMATES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Changes in Accounting Estimates — Prospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Identical prospective treatment to IAS 8</div><div class="text-supporting">Changes in estimates (e.g. useful life revisions, bad debt provision changes) are recognised PROSPECTIVELY in the period of change and future periods — IDENTICAL to IAS 8, with NO restatement of prior periods.</div></div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 6 — PRIOR PERIOD ERRORS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Prior Period Errors — Retrospective Restatement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Identical to IAS 8</div><div class="text-supporting">Material prior period errors are corrected RETROSPECTIVELY in the first financial statements authorised for issue after discovery, by restating comparative amounts, or if the error occurred before the earliest period presented, by restating opening balances — IDENTICAL to IAS 8.</div></div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 7 — INDIAN RESTATEMENT PRACTICE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Indian Restatement Practice &amp; Schedule III Interaction</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A practical presentation-layer consideration</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">When restating comparatives for policy changes/errors, Indian companies must present the restated figures WITHIN Schedule III's mandatory format (see Ind AS 1), including a THIRD balance sheet (as of the beginning of the earliest comparative period) where retrospective restatement has a material effect — an application of Ind AS 8's own IDENTICAL "third balance sheet" requirement (shared with IAS 8/IAS 1) within India's specific presentation format.</div>
    </div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 8 — IMPRACTICABILITY EXCEPTION ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Impracticability Exception</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Identical to IAS 8</div><div class="text-supporting">Where retrospective application/restatement is IMPRACTICABLE (e.g. effects cannot be reasonably determined despite every reasonable effort), the entity applies the new policy/correction prospectively from the earliest practicable date — IDENTICAL exception to IAS 8.</div></div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 9 — DISCLOSURE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Identical disclosure requirements to IAS 8</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and reason for accounting policy changes</span><span>Amount of adjustment for each financial statement line item affected</span><span>Nature and amount of estimate changes with a material current/future effect</span><span>Nature of prior period errors and correction amounts</span></div></div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 10 — JUDGMENTS & ESTIMATES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where management judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Distinguishing a change in estimate from a change in policy (a genuinely common source of practical difficulty)</span><span>Materiality assessment for prior period errors</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Quantifying the cumulative retrospective adjustment for policy changes/errors</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="callout warn callout--warn-flush">A change resulting from NEW INFORMATION about an asset's condition (e.g. revised useful life based on updated usage patterns) is a change in ESTIMATE, not policy — a distinction requiring careful judgement, IDENTICAL to the analysis required under IAS 8.</div>
    </div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 11 — IND AS 8 vs IAS 8 ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Ind AS 8 vs IAS 8 — Full Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comprehensive comparison table</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>IAS 8</span><span>Ind AS 8</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Policy hierarchy, retrospective/prospective treatment</span><span>Standard model</span><span>IDENTICAL — no substantive divergence</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Third balance sheet presentation</span><span>Required where material</span><span>IDENTICAL, presented within Schedule III's mandatory format</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">Ind AS 8 is essentially IDENTICAL to IAS 8 in substance — its Indian practical relevance is confined to how restatements are PRESENTED within Schedule III's format, not any divergence in the underlying accounting treatment.</div>
    </div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 12 — STATEMENT MAPPING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Comprehensive event-to-statement mapping table</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event / transaction</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Retrospective policy change adjustment</span><span><span class="badge be">Equity</span> (opening retained earnings) <span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>Comparatives restated</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Estimate change</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Current and future periods only</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Prior period error correction</span><span><span class="badge be">Equity</span> <span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>Comparatives restated, third balance sheet where material</span></div>
      </div>
    </div></div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 13 — RELATED STANDARDS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IAS 8</span><span>The global counterpart standard, near-identically converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>Ind AS 1</span><span>Provides the presentation format (Schedule III) within which restatements are shown</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>Ind AS 10</span><span>Distinguishes error correction from adjusting/non-adjusting events after the reporting period</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn"><div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Third balance sheet</div><div class="glossary-def">An additional balance sheet as at the beginning of the earliest comparative period, required when retrospective restatement has a material effect — identical to IAS 8/IAS 1.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Impracticable</div><div class="glossary-def">A requirement cannot be applied after every reasonable effort — identical threshold to IAS 8.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 14 — GLOSSARY ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Prior period errors", definition: "Omissions/misstatements from failure to use, or misuse of, reliable information available when prior period statements were authorised for issue — identical to IAS 8." },
      { term: "Retrospective application", definition: "Applying a new policy as if it had always been applied — identical concept to IAS 8." },
      { term: "Third balance sheet", definition: "An additional balance sheet as at the beginning of the earliest comparative period, required when retrospective restatement has a material effect — identical to IAS 8/IAS 1." },
      { term: "Impracticable", definition: "A requirement cannot be applied after every reasonable effort — identical threshold to IAS 8." },
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
